  "name": "r-history-citing-an-authority-no-commit-installs",
  "note": "What is sent with history is everything it reaches, and a commit reaches the authority it cites. Authority 1 is a successor of the genesis that no commit installs; H.3 lets c1 cite it all the same, since it descends from what c1's parent put in effect. The source's current authority is still the genesis. A reader asking for c1 is sent authority 1 with it, through that citation and nothing else, and records both commits.",
